    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1134">

                <pb facs="1433" n="1423" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.9327/11–547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-05T17:00:00+08:00">November 5, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 6—3:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2197. As suggested Shanghai’s 1699, October 23, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1134-f1"/> (relayed through Nanking), Embassy has now received note
                    from Minister of Foreign Affairs dated October 29, 1947 as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“An official letter has just been received from the Minister of Commerce
                                [<hi rendition="#italic">Communications</hi>] stating that as the
                            revision of the Sino-American Air Transport Agreement<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d1134-f2"/> with respect to a number of questions in
                            connection with details of traffic operations is most desirable, it is
                            requested, pursuant to the provisions of article XI of the agreement,
                            the competent U. S. aeronautical authorities be approached to depute an
                            officer to consult with that Ministry for the revision.</p>
                        <p>“The above is communicated to the Embassy for its attention and action,
                            and the favor of a reply will be appreciated.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Department will recall that article XI of Sino-American Bilateral Air Transport
                    Agreement calls for commencement consultation provided for therein within period
                    60 days from date of request which in this case is October 29, 1947. Embassy has
                    informed Minister of Foreign Affairs that text Minister’s note has been
                    forwarded Department and that Embassy will communicate further with Minister
                    when instructions received.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2197, repeated Shanghai 868.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1134-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1134-f1-content">
